1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,622
Day 49: OpenWorker, an AI coworker published on Andrew Ng's

2
00:00:04,622 --> 00:00:08,382
GitHub, run on local Qwen models through Ollama.

3
00:00:08,832 --> 00:00:10,411
It works in your files.

4
00:00:10,411 --> 00:00:13,293
Every tool call needs approval by default,

5
00:00:13,293 --> 00:00:15,764
and every call is logged either way.

6
00:00:16,214 --> 00:00:20,863
We ran the CLI headless and isolated from real settings,

7
00:00:20,863 --> 00:00:24,766
pointed at Ollama serving Qwen 2.5 at 7, 14 and

8
00:00:24,766 --> 00:00:26,593
32 billion parameters.

9
00:00:27,043 --> 00:00:30,005
When the model calls a tool like write_file,

10
00:00:30,005 --> 00:00:31,755
the approval gate decides.

11
00:00:31,755 --> 00:00:33,708
In ask mode with no terminal,

12
00:00:33,708 --> 00:00:36,064
the call is refused before it runs.

13
00:00:36,514 --> 00:00:40,592
Approved or denied, every call lands in a SQLite audit log.

14
00:00:40,592 --> 00:00:42,597
Even with approvals bypassed,

15
00:00:42,597 --> 00:00:45,500
writes outside the workspace were blocked.

16
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:50,790
On the README task, turning two meeting notes into a brief,

17
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:54,891
14B succeeded three times out of five and 7B once.

18
00:00:54,891 --> 00:00:57,188
The largest, 32B, never did:

19
00:00:57,188 --> 00:01:02,192
it searched for files named meeting, found none, and gave up.

20
00:01:02,642 --> 00:01:05,039
All fifteen runs reported completed.

21
00:01:05,039 --> 00:01:09,167
The gate held; the outcome flag did not mean the job was done.
